## Abstract

Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) offers significant potential for legal AI, yet systematic benchmarks are sparse. Prior work introduced LaborBench to benchmark RAG models based on ostensible ground truth from an exhaustive, multi-month, manual enumeration of all U.S. state unemployment insurance requirements by U.S. Fifth, we chart the path forward for legal RAG through concrete design principles, offering actionable guidance for building AI systems capable of accurate multi-jurisdictional legal research.

